"During a recent MPLS VPN deployment using Nokia 7750 SR routers, we need to ensure strict control over BGP route acceptance to prevent unauthorized route propagation. What's the recommended approach to filter incoming BGP updates so the router only installs routes carrying either the route target communities target:192.0.2.10:100 (for our customer VPN) or target:64496:200 (for the management VPN), while explicitly rejecting all other routes?"
