## User question:
"During a recent network upgrade, we're implementing segment routing across our core infrastructure using Nokia 7750 SR routers, and I need to ensure BGP is properly configured to propagate our locally defined SR policies to external peers. Specifically, how should I set up BGP to treat these segment routing policies as self-originated routes and distribute them via the SR policy IPv4 AFI to neighboring routers that support this capability?"
---
## Proposed answer:
/configure router policy-options policy-statement "export-sr-policy" entry 10 from protocol static
/configure router policy-options policy-statement "export-sr-policy" entry 10 action accept
/configure router bgp group "external-peers" family sr-policy-ipv4 export "export-sr-policy"
---
