## User question:
"During a recent MPLS VPN deployment using Nokia 7750 SR routers, we need to ensure efficient route distribution while maintaining control over path advertisements. What would be the appropriate configuration approach to limit BGP to propagating a maximum of eight VPNv4 routes per NLRI update, while also ensuring the router won't accept any incoming VPN-IPv4 routes from peers?"
---
## Proposed answer:
configure router bgp group <group-name> family vpn-ipv4 prefix-limit export 8
configure router bgp group <group-name> family vpn-ipv4 maximum-routes 0 action idle
